It uses the helper functions you have in the toolset (`createTypingSVG`, `setTypingAnimation`, `customizeDeletionAnimation`, `pauseTypingAnimation`, and `setCursorBlinkRate`) so you don’t need any third‑party libraries.

---

## 1️⃣ What the animation will do

| Moment | Visual effect |
|--------|----------------|
| **Page load** | A placeholder‑style SVG “typing” animation runs once, showing the user what to type. |
| **User starts typing** | The SVG pauses, the real `<input>`/`<textarea>` gains focus, and the cursor starts blinking. |
| **User deletes everything** | The SVG “deletes” the text at a configurable speed, then re‑plays the placeholder after a short pause. |
| **Form submit / blur** | The animation stops (or you can let it keep looping). |

---

## 2️⃣ HTML – Minimal markup

```html
<form id="contactForm">
  <div class="field-wrapper" data-placeholder="Your name…">
    <input type="text" name="name" id="nameInput" autocomplete="off" />
  </div>

  <div class="field-wrapper" data-placeholder="Your email address…">
    <input type="email" name="email" id="emailInput" autocomplete="off" />
  </div>

  <div class="field-wrapper" data-placeholder="Your message…">
    <textarea name="message" id="messageInput" rows="4"></textarea>
  </div>

  <button type="submit">Send</button>
</form>
```

*Each `.field-wrapper` holds the real input **and** the SVG that will be generated for the placeholder animation.*  
The `data-placeholder` attribute contains the text you want the animation to type out.

---

## 3️⃣ CSS – Position the SVG over the input

```css
.field-wrapper {
  position: relative;
  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}

/* Hide the native placeholder (we’ll use the SVG instead) */
.field-wrapper input,
.field-wrapper textarea {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
  font-size: 1rem;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* The SVG sits on top of the input until the user focuses */
.field-wrapper .typing-svg {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  pointer-events: none;   /* let clicks go through to the input */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  padding-left: 0.8rem;   /* same as input padding */
  color: #777;            /* placeholder colour */
  font-family: sans-serif;
  font-size: 1rem;
}
```

---

## 4️⃣ JavaScript – Glue everything together

```html
<script type="module">
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 1️⃣ Helper: create a typing‑SVG for a given wrapper
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  function addTypingSVG(wrapper, text) {
    // Create the SVG (the function returns an <svg> element)
    const svg = await createTypingSVG({
      text,
      fontColor: '#777',
      fontFamily: 'sans-serif',
      fontSize: 16,
      typingSpeed: 120   // words‑per‑minute (feel free to tweak)
    });

    // Give it a predictable ID so we can address it later
    const svgId = `typing-${Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9)}`;
    svg.id = svgId;
    svg.classList.add('typing-svg');

    // Insert it as the first child of the wrapper
    wrapper.prepend(svg);

    // Return the ID for later control
    return svgId;
  }

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 2️⃣ Initialise every .field‑wrapper on the page
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  document.querySelectorAll('.field-wrapper').forEach(async wrapper => {
    const placeholder = wrapper.dataset.placeholder || '';
    if (!placeholder) return;   // nothing to animate

    // 1️⃣ Create the SVG and store its ID
    const svgId = await addTypingSVG(wrapper, placeholder);

    // 2️⃣ Set global typing speed (optional – you can also set per‑field)
    setTypingAnimation({ typingSpeed: 120, delayBeforeStart: 500 });

    // 3️⃣ Configure deletion (when the user clears the field)
    customizeDeletionAnimation({ deletionSpeed: 180, pauseBeforeRetyping: 800 });

    // 4️⃣ Cursor blink rate (nice finishing touch)
    setCursorBlinkRate({ blinkRate: '600', svgId });

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 5️⃣ Wire up focus / input / blur events
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    const input = wrapper.querySelector('input, textarea');

    // When the user focuses, pause the placeholder animation
    input.addEventListener('focus', () => {
      pauseTypingAnimation({ pauseDuration: '999999', svgId }); // effectively pause
    });

    // When the user starts typing, hide the SVG (so the real caret shows)
    input.addEventListener('input', () => {
      const svg = document.getElementById(svgId);
      if (input.value.length > 0) {
        svg.style.display = 'none';
      } else {
        // If they delete everything, bring the SVG back after a short pause
        setTimeout(() => {
          svg.style.display = 'flex';
          // Restart the typing animation from the beginning
          pauseTypingAnimation({ pauseDuration: '0', svgId });
        }, 500);
      }
    });

    // When the field loses focus and is empty, resume the placeholder
    input.addEventListener('blur', () => {
      if (input.value.trim() === '') {
        const svg = document.getElementById(svgId);
        svg.style.display = 'flex';
        pauseTypingAnimation({ pauseDuration: '0', svgId });
      }
    });
  });
</script>
```

### What the script does, step‑by‑step

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| **Create SVG** | Calls `createTypingSVG` with the placeholder text and stores the generated `<svg>` inside the wrapper. |
| **Set typing speed** | `setTypingAnimation` defines how fast the “typing” runs (words‑per‑minute) and an optional start delay. |
| **Configure deletion** | `customizeDeletionAnimation` tells the animation how fast to erase characters when the user clears the field, plus a pause before it starts typing again. |
| **Cursor blink** | `setCursorBlinkRate` makes the simulated cursor blink at a comfortable rate (600 ms in the example). |
| **Focus** | When the real input receives focus, we pause the SVG so the native caret can appear. |
| **Input** | As soon as the user types any character, we hide the SVG (so the native caret isn’t overlapped). If they delete everything, we bring the SVG back after a short timeout. |
| **Blur** | If the field loses focus while empty, the placeholder animation restarts automatically. |

---

## 5️⃣ Tweaking the experience

| Need | How to adjust |
|------|----------------|
| **Faster typing** | Increase `typingSpeed` in `setTypingAnimation` (e.g., `180`). |
| **Slower deletion** | Lower `deletionSpeed` in `customizeDeletionAnimation`. |
| **Longer pause before the placeholder re‑appears** | Change the `setTimeout` delay in the `input` listener (default `500 ms`). |
| **Different colour / font** | Pass `fontColor`, `fontFamily`, `fontSize` to `createTypingSVG`. |
| **Only run once (no looping)** | After the first run, call `pauseTypingAnimation({ pauseDuration: '999999', svgId })` to freeze it. |
| **Multiple languages** | Provide the placeholder text in the appropriate language; the SVG will render any Unicode characters. |

---

## 6️⃣ Full‑page example (copy‑paste)

```html
